            <fr:title text="Five sigils make any dialect readable">Five sigils make any dialect readable</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Card</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="anki">1787404869020</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="anki-deck">MLSys</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
  <html:p>What do the five <fr:link href="/IR7B/" title="MLIR" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/IR7B/" display-uri="IR7B" type="local">MLIR</fr:link> sigils <html:code><![CDATA[%]]></html:code>, <html:code>^</html:code>, <html:code>@</html:code>, <html:code><![CDATA[#]]></html:code>, <html:code>!</html:code> mark?</html:p>
  
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);">Answer</html:span></html:summary>
  <html:ul><html:li><html:code><![CDATA[%]]></html:code> — an <fr:link href="/4SV9/" title="Static single assignment" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/4SV9/" display-uri="4SV9" type="local">Static single assignment</fr:link> value (<fr:link href="/MOVC/" title="SSA names are printing hints" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/MOVC/" display-uri="MOVC" type="local"><fr:link href="/4SV9/" title="Static single assignment" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/4SV9/" display-uri="4SV9" type="local">SSA</fr:link> names are printing hints</fr:link>).</html:li>
    <html:li><html:code>^</html:code> — a block label (<fr:link href="/QZFU/" title="Block arguments replace phi nodes" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/QZFU/" display-uri="QZFU" type="local">Block arguments replace phi nodes</fr:link>).</html:li>
    <html:li><html:code>@</html:code> — a symbol: function, global (<fr:link href="/45LB/" title="Symbols are looked up, values are defined" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/45LB/" display-uri="45LB" type="local">Symbols are looked up, values are defined</fr:link>).</html:li>
    <html:li><html:code><![CDATA[#]]></html:code> — an attribute or attribute alias: <html:code><![CDATA[#map0]]></html:code>, <html:code><![CDATA[#stablehlo.dot<...>]]></html:code>, <html:code><![CDATA[#tpu.memory_space<vmem>]]></html:code>.</html:li>
    <html:li><html:code>!</html:code> — a type or type alias: <html:code><![CDATA[!llvm.ptr]]></html:code>, <html:code><![CDATA[!tt.ptr<f32>]]></html:code>.</html:li></html:ul>

  <html:strong>This is the whole trick to reading an unfamiliar dialect.</html:strong> <fr:link href="/IR7B/" title="MLIR" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/IR7B/" display-uri="IR7B" type="local">MLIR</fr:link> is extensible in ops, types, and attributes, so you will constantly meet names you do not know — but the sigil tells you <html:em>which kind of thing</html:em> it is, and therefore where it may legally appear. <html:code><![CDATA[#]]></html:code> and <html:code>!</html:code> in particular are the escape hatches every dialect uses for its own metadata (<fr:link href="/9N7G/" title="The prefix says which side of layout assignment" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/9N7G/" display-uri="9N7G" type="local">The prefix says which side of layout assignment</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/64A0/" title="Mosaic is explicit memory spaces and explicit copies" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/64A0/" display-uri="64A0" type="local"><fr:link href="/M3MH/" title="Mosaic" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/M3MH/" display-uri="M3MH" type="local">Mosaic</fr:link> is explicit memory spaces and explicit copies</fr:link>).
</html:details>
</html:div>



</fr:mainmatter>
